#: scripts/junction_room.gd:875
msgid "RELIEF VENT"
msgstr "СБРОСНОЙ КЛАПАН"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: Station plate (12-13 px label on a machine). ALL CAPS, as short as possible. The pressure line's handwheel valve, before the breaker is armed.
#. i18n: speaker=ui
#: scripts/junction_room.gd:877
#: scripts/junction_room.gd:1552
msgid "VALVE"
msgstr "ВЕНТИЛЬ"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: Station plate (12-13 px label on a machine). ALL CAPS, as short as possible. A placard over the sealed blast door the pressure line can blow open.
#. i18n: speaker=ui
#: scripts/junction_room.gd:879
#: scripts/junction_room.gd:1571
msgid "SEALED DOOR"
msgstr "ДВЕРЬ ЗАПЕЧАТАНА"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: Station plate (12-13 px label on a machine). ALL CAPS, as short as possible. The lever that drops the hanging coolant tank; the hints name it with the same words.
#. i18n: speaker=ui
#: scripts/junction_room.gd:881
#: scripts/junction_room.gd:1575
msgid "TANK RELEASE"
msgstr "ОТЦЕПКА БАКА"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: Station plate (12-13 px label on a machine). ALL CAPS, as short as possible. Over the dropped coolant tank once it lies on the floor.
#. i18n: speaker=ui
#: scripts/junction_room.gd:883
msgid "TANK DOWN"
msgstr "БАК СБРОШЕН"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: Station plate (12-13 px label on a machine). ALL CAPS, as short as possible. The caption by the Service Junction's pressure line dial.
#. i18n: speaker=ui
#: scripts/junction_room.gd:886
msgid "LINE"
msgstr "ЛИНИЯ"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: Station plate (12-13 px label on a machine). ALL CAPS, as short as possible. The junction's valve after the blast used the line up. Cut to fit: ВЕНТИЛЬ ОТРАБОТАН and ВЕНТИЛЬ ПУСТ ran into DOOR DOWN, so the plate on the valve says only ОТРАБОТАН (used up), as the breaker's does. Not ВЕНТ. (reads as the relief vent or ventilation), ВЕНТИЛЬ ИСП. (3 px too wide, and ИСП. read back as исправен, OK) or ВЕНТИЛЬ ВСЁ (read back as VALVE ALL).
#. i18n: speaker=ui
#: scripts/junction_room.gd:1547
msgid "VALVE USED"
msgstr "ОТРАБОТАН"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: Station plate (12-13 px label on a machine). ALL CAPS, as short as possible. The valve's plate once the pressure charge is set and its fuse burns; the same words open a hint.
#. i18n: speaker=ui
#: scripts/junction_room.gd:1549
msgid "FUSE LIT"
msgstr "ФИТИЛЬ ГОРИТ"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: Station plate (12-13 px label on a machine). ALL CAPS, as short as possible. The valve's plate while it is cranked: turns done of turns needed ("VALVE  3 / 8"). Keep both %d and the two spaces before them.
#. i18n: speaker=ui
#: scripts/junction_room.gd:1551
#, c-format
msgid "VALVE  %d / %d"
msgstr "ВЕНТИЛЬ  %d / %d"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: Station plate (12-13 px label on a machine). ALL CAPS, as short as possible. The junction's breaker after the blast used the line up. Cut to fit: РУБИЛЬНИК ОТРАБОТАН ran into RELIEF VENT, so the plate on the breaker says only ОТРАБОТАН (used up), as the valve's does. Not ВЫКЛ. (off, which invites switching it back on), ИСП. (read back as исправен, OK) or ОТРАБ. (read back as tripped).
#. i18n: speaker=ui
#: scripts/junction_room.gd:1560
msgid "BREAKER USED"
msgstr "ОТРАБОТАН"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: Station plate (12-13 px label on a machine). ALL CAPS, as short as possible. The overload breaker after the pressure line tripped it (it cut out).
#. i18n: speaker=ui
#: scripts/junction_room.gd:1566
msgid "BREAKER TRIPPED"
msgstr "РУБИЛЬНИК СРАБОТАЛ"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: Station plate (12-13 px label on a machine). ALL CAPS, as short as possible. The overload breaker once armed: the line has power.
#. i18n: speaker=ui
#: scripts/junction_room.gd:1566
msgid "BREAKER LIVE"
msgstr "РУБИЛЬНИК ВКЛЮЧЁН"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: Station plate (12-13 px label on a machine). ALL CAPS, as short as possible. The blast door's placard after the blast threw the door out of its frame.
#. i18n: speaker=ui
#: scripts/junction_room.gd:1571
msgid "DOOR DOWN"
msgstr "ДВЕРЬ ВЫБИТА"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: Station plate (12-13 px label on a machine). ALL CAPS, as short as possible. The TANK RELEASE lever's plate once its tank has been dropped for good.
#. i18n: speaker=ui
#: scripts/junction_room.gd:1575
msgid "RELEASE USED"
msgstr "ОТЦЕПКА ОТРАБОТАНА"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: Station plate (12-13 px label on a machine). ALL CAPS, as short as possible. The TANK RELEASE lever's plate while the winch hauls a missed tank back up to its clamp.
#. i18n: speaker=ui
#: scripts/junction_room.gd:1575
msgid "WINCHING UP"
msgstr "ПОДЪЁМ БАКА"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: Station plate (12-13 px label on a machine). ALL CAPS, as short as possible. The junction's exit hatch, open.
